  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the highest-value first experiment is to establish the simplest possible baseline: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA-2000 (config_001). This gives a reference validation accuracy against which all subsequent complexity additions (multiprofile aggregation, learned encoders, image modality, multimodal fusion) can be measured. PCA is a cheap, well-understood encoder that avoids confounding the baseline with encoder-specific effects. Starting here lets me then isolate the marginal contribution of each design axis in subsequent experiments: (1) multiprofile+aggregation vs singleprofile, (2) image-only vs RNA-only, (3) multimodal fusion vs best single modality, and (4) encoder choice. Under a 10-experiment budget, anchoring to the simplest configuration first maximizes interpretability of every later comparison and avoids prematurely committing to a complex multimodal setup whose individual components are unvalidated."
}

